    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "The architects of policy faced a failure of the creative process, as a funding dispute persisted in the reconciliation package. This government impasse left the enforcement apparatus of a federal law enforcement agency operating without full legislative support, even as the spring weather changed. Security analysts observed the immigration statistics, noting how the increase in apprehensions reflected a border activity metric caught between the rigid system's goals and the affected population it sought to process.",
