    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "Along the U.S. border, the border security agency of the U.S. government entity faced a shift in the geopolitical region. The environmental factor of spring weather invited movement, leading to a clear pattern emerged in the numbers of those crossing the border. Policy observers, as pattern-finders, noted the low crossing numbers that formed an enforcement policy outcome, while the builders of a new framework in government struggled to translate this statistical trend into a coherent design.",
